 <17342133+angelrenefm@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 19:27:21 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] media: s5p-mfc: register the encoder on MFC v15
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

With the previous commits the encoder works on the Pixel 7. Through
GStreamer's v4l2h264enc, v4l2h265enc and v4l2vp8enc, 60 frame 1080p
clips are complete in 18 runs out of 18, 90 frame 3840x2160 clips at
20 Mbit/s too, and 1 and 4 Mbit/s asked are met. Through FFmpeg's
*_v4l2m2m encoders at 4 Mbit/s, 720p, PSNR against the source is about
43 dB for H.264, HEVC and VP8.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Ángel René <17342133+angelrenefm@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/media/platform/samsung/s5p-mfc/s5p_mfc.c | 12 ------------
 1 file changed, 12 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/samsung/s5p-mfc/s5p_mfc.c b/drivers/media/platform/samsung/s5p-mfc/s5p_mfc.c
index 1a0b56454..b51e4e2d1 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/samsung/s5p-mfc/s5p_mfc.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/samsung/s5p-mfc/s5p_mfc.c
@@ -1475,18 +1475,6 @@ static int s5p_mfc_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	v4l2_info(&dev->v4l2_dev,
 		  "decoder registered as /dev/video%d\n", dev->vfd_dec->num);
 
-	/*
-	 * The v15 encoder's registers differ from v12's (0xF770/0xF774 clash
-	 * with the decoder's) and nothing here programs them yet: no encoder
-	 * node rather than one that hangs the firmware.
-	 */
-	if (IS_MFCV15(dev)) {
-		video_device_release(dev->vfd_enc);
-		dev->vfd_enc = NULL;
-		pr_debug("%s--\n", __func__);
-		return 0;
-	}
-
 	ret = video_register_device(dev->vfd_enc, VFL_TYPE_VIDEO, 0);
 	if (ret) {
 		v4l2_err(&dev->v4l2_dev, "Failed to register video device\n");
